    "certs": "Angular (Intermediate) Certificate\nAngular (Basic) Certificate\nResponsive Web Design\nMTA Database Administration\nFundamentals \nMTA introduction to programming\nusing python Bilel Feki Dit Kaaniche\nFull-Stack Developer | Java & Angular Specialist | Passionate About\nCybersecurity & DevOps | Aspiring Software Architect\nTunis, Tunisia\nRésumé\nI’m Belal, a dedicated full-stack developer from Tunisia, aspiring\nto be a software architect. I thrive on innovation and excellence,\nleveraging Java (Spring Boot) and Angular to craft dynamic, robust\nweb applications. My deep enthusiasm for RxJS ensures that every\nproject I undertake is not only efficient and scalable but also highly\ninteractive and responsive. Driven by a commitment to quality and\ncontinuous improvement, I approach development with a focus on\ncutting-edge technology and seamless user experiences. Each\nproject I work on is a step toward realizing my goal of becoming a\nleading software architect.\nExpérience\nInfor\nSoftware Engineer\ndécembre 2025 - Present  (3 mois)\nAdvanced Derivative Solutions\nFull Stack Engineer \njuillet 2023 - Present  (2 ans 8 mois)\nTunis, Tunisia\n* Designed and implemented a Java library for tracking outbound emails sent\nfrom a Spring Boot application using the JavaMail API.\nEstablished connection to the OVH SMTP server via Spring Mail for secure\nand reliable email delivery.\nRetrieved and parsed undelivered email reports using Oracle’s JavaMail API to\nidentify bouncebacks.\n  Page 1 of 3\n   \nIntegrated Quartz Scheduler to automate inbox polling and retry logic, ensuring\nmessage delivery success.\nBuilt a resilient retry mechanism to resend failed emails under defined failure\nconditions automatically.\n* Developed a filter persistence feature for an Angular-based front-end\napplication.\nEnabled users to save and reuse customized filters by storing Angular\nFormGroup states in a relational database.\nEnsured dynamic pre-filling of saved filter forms, enhancing UX with\npersonalized and reusable search configurations.\n* Collaborated using Git version control within a pull request (PR)-based\nworkflow:\nCreated and managed feature branches, regularly committing changes with\ndescriptive messages.\nSubmitted and reviewed pull requests to ensure high code quality and\nconsistency with team standards.\nResolved merge conflicts and contributed to peer code reviews as part of a\ncollaborative development process\nInstitut Supérieur des Etudes Technologiques en Communications\nde Tunis\nInstructor\nseptembre 2023 "
